  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "An equilateral triangle has sides length $1+\\sqrt3$. Find:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the perimeter of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3+3\\sqrt3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=3(1+\\sqrt3)\\\\P&=3+3\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the area of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt3+\\frac32$\n\nDraw the altitude and use Pythagoras to find the perpendicular height.",
          "worked": "The altitude bisects the base. Let the perpendicular height be $h$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=(1+\\sqrt3)^2-\\left(\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2\\\\h^2&=\\frac34(1+\\sqrt3)^2\\\\h&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}(1+\\sqrt3)\\\\h&=\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(1+\\sqrt3)\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{3+\\sqrt3+3\\sqrt3+3}{4}\\\\A&=\\sqrt3+\\frac32\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      }
    ]
  },
